{"id":"qd9pda6DDomNZqxQ","meta":{"instanceId":"9f24379abd1ca05a3f590fdaa874ca82fbc5e1188798d609d51d2a8f6bacb662"},"name":"Procurement Metrics Benchmarking Workflow (Procurement Industry)","tags":[],"nodes":[{"id":"bdb3c168-ea20-4cce-a9a1-8f3ae28b1bcc","name":"Monthly KPI Benchmark Trigger","type":"n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger","position":[-3648,992],"parameters":{"rule":{"interval":[{"field":"months","triggerAtHour":9}]}},"typeVersion":1.3},{"id":"55031ffe-a4eb-464c-bc70-23dde4739ccd","name":"Load Benchmark Settings","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[-3408,992],"parameters":{"options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"f6b6a27b-96d9-44ad-b6bb-f42653f6df32","name":"ready_status","type":"string","value":"Ready"},{"id":"256298d2-b064-4e36-80a1-59755748177a","name":"processed_status","type":"string","value":"Processed"},{"id":"1639c79a-37d8-4983-8698-9bb8ccc86257","name":"active_benchmark_value","type":"string","value":"Yes"},{"id":"9ddb12fc-7f46-48b4-8363-201e313d47d3","name":"active_kpi_definition_value","type":"string","value":"Yes"},{"id":"a1f281ab-66db-4322-9a81-da779e6b2fff","name":"near_benchmark_threshold_pct","type":"number","value":5},{"id":"7901d4b0-d296-4d45-8108-7db118b58904","name":"max_recommendations","type":"number","value":3},{"id":"904a9c29-7181-4d9c-899c-4a1389339c9f","name":"report_status_completed","type":"string","value":"Completed"},{"id":"1857643e-1b0a-4cab-adfb-eef33629baa6","name":"review_required_status","type":"string","value":"Review Required"},{"id":"98e7b664-b9b3-4614-bd90-3a2dfd07086f","name":"leadership_email","type":"string","value":""},{"id":"0a7d20a9-5d4a-4fe7-a103-aee4aa36c552","name":"monthly_report_email","type":"string","value":""},{"id":"899e7158-5fec-40c4-8895-4534a78548b7","name":"alert_open_status","type":"string","value":"Open"},{"id":"607e0365-22af-498e-a84d-9c9a29d54ab5","name":"missing_definition_message","type":"string","value":"No active KPI definition was found for this KPI"},{"id":"b9c02d0b-5638-45d7-8943-fd470fd858ac","name":"missing_benchmark_message","type":"string","value":"No active external benchmark was found for this KPI."},{"id":"88f5a5f9-a7e5-4e0b-a1d4-0107ece6cdc2","name":"report_title_prefix","type":"string","value":"Procurement KPI Benchmark Report"}]}},"typeVersion":3.4},{"id":"be494567-5738-415d-a9e9-47d9a997e704","name":"Get KPI Definition","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","position":[-2800,992],"parameters":{"options":{},"filtersUI":{"values":[{"lookupValue":"={{ $json.kpi_code }}","lookupColumn":"kpi_code"},{"lookupValue":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.active_kpi_definition_value }}","lookupColumn":"active"}]},"sheetName":{"__rl":true,"mode":"list","value":2068041816,"cachedResultUrl":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY/edit#gid=2068041816","cachedResultName":"KPI_Definitions"},"documentId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"list","value":"1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY","cachedResultUrl":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY/edit?usp=drivesdk","cachedResultName":"Procurement_KPI_Benchmarking_Mock_Data"}},"typeVersion":4.7,"alwaysOutputData":true},{"id":"36370f9c-3251-4d08-a486-e4a05301a1f5","name":"Get External Benchmark","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","position":[-2352,832],"parameters":{"options":{},"filtersUI":{"values":[{"lookupValue":"={{ $json.kpi_code }}","lookupColumn":"kpi_code"},{"lookupValue":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.active_benchmark_value }}","lookupColumn":"active"}]},"sheetName":{"__rl":true,"mode":"list","value":65023634,"cachedResultUrl":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY/edit#gid=65023634","cachedResultName":"External_Benchmarks"},"documentId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"list","value":"1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY","cachedResultUrl":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY/edit?usp=drivesdk","cachedResultName":"Procurement_KPI_Benchmarking_Mock_Data"}},"typeVersion":4.7,"alwaysOutputData":true},{"id":"067f0175-2aac-42fc-a447-c2b873b9d4c3","name":"Build Benchmark Comparison Context","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[-1680,624],"parameters":{"mode":"runOnceForEachItem","jsCode":"const benchmark = $json;\n\nconst kpi = $('Get Ready Procurement KPIs').item.json;\nconst definition = $('Get KPI Definition').item.json;\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    kpi_record_id: kpi.kpi_record_id,\n    kpi_code: kpi.kpi_code,\n    kpi_name: kpi.kpi_name,\n    period: kpi.period,\n    business_unit: kpi.business_unit,\n\n    actual_value: Number(kpi.actual_value),\n    target_value: Number(kpi.target_value),\n    unit: kpi.unit,\n    data_source: kpi.data_source,\n\n    direction: definition.direction,\n    description: definition.description,\n    warning_threshold_pct: Number(definition.warning_threshold_pct),\n    critical_threshold_pct: Number(definition.critical_threshold_pct),\n\n    benchmark_id: benchmark.benchmark_id,\n    peer_group: benchmark.peer_group,\n    benchmark_value: Number(benchmark.benchmark_value),\n    benchmark_period: benchmark.benchmark_period,\n    benchmark_source: benchmark.source_name,\n    benchmark_confidence: benchmark.benchmark_confidence\n  }\n};"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"c8e66361-7d7f-469b-8ae6-41534a5846fc","name":"Calculate Benchmark Gap","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[-896,608],"parameters":{"mode":"runOnceForEachItem","jsCode":"const item = $json;\n\nconst actual = Number(item.actual_value);\nconst benchmark = Number(item.benchmark_value);\n\nconst direction = String(item.direction || '').trim();\n\nconst warningThreshold = Number(item.warning_threshold_pct || 0);\nconst criticalThreshold = Number(item.critical_threshold_pct || 0);\n\nconst nearThreshold =\n  Number(\n    $('Load Benchmark Settings')\n      .first()\n      .json\n      .near_benchmark_threshold_pct\n  ) || 5;\n\n// Raw numerical difference\nconst absoluteGap = actual - benchmark;\n\n// Percentage difference relative to benchmark\nconst rawGapPercentage =\n  benchmark !== 0\n    ? (Math.abs(actual - benchmark) / Math.abs(benchmark)) * 100\n    : 0;\n\n// Determine whether actual performance is better or worse\nlet isBetter = false;\nlet isWorse = false;\n\nif (direction === 'Higher Is Better') {\n  isBetter = actual > benchmark;\n  isWorse = actual < benchmark;\n}\n\nif (direction === 'Lower Is Better') {\n  isBetter = actual < benchmark;\n  isWorse = actual > benchmark;\n}\n\n// Performance classification\nlet performanceStatus = 'Near Benchmark';\n\nif (rawGapPercentage <= nearThreshold) {\n  performanceStatus = 'Near Benchmark';\n} else if (isBetter) {\n  performanceStatus = 'Above Benchmark';\n} else if (isWorse) {\n  performanceStatus = 'Below Benchmark';\n}\n\n// Severity should only increase when performance is worse\nlet severity = 'Low';\n\nif (isWorse) {\n  if (rawGapPercentage >= criticalThreshold) {\n    severity = 'Critical';\n  } else if (rawGapPercentage >= warningThreshold) {\n    severity = 'High';\n  } else if (rawGapPercentage > nearThreshold) {\n    severity = 'Medium';\n  }\n}\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...item,\n\n    absolute_gap: Number(absoluteGap.toFixed(2)),\n    gap_percentage: Number(rawGapPercentage.toFixed(2)),\n\n    performance_status: performanceStatus,\n    severity,\n\n    benchmark_gap_detected:\n      performanceStatus === 'Below Benchmark'\n  }\n};"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"ced67288-f714-413d-9b3b-639480bafa9e","name":"Generate KPI Gap Analysis","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm","position":[-480,608],"parameters":{"text":"=Analyze the following procurement KPI.\n\nKPI Code:\n{{ $json.kpi_code }}\n\nKPI Name:\n{{ $json.kpi_name }}\n\nDescription:\n{{ $json.description }}\n\nBusiness Unit:\n{{ $json.business_unit }}\n\nReporting Period:\n{{ $json.period }}\n\nActual Value:\n{{ $json.actual_value }} {{ $json.unit }}\n\nKPI Target:\n{{ $json.target_value }} {{ $json.unit }}\n\nExternal Benchmark:\n{{ $json.benchmark_value }} {{ $json.unit }}\n\nBenchmark Peer Group:\n{{ $json.peer_group }}\n\nBenchmark Source:\n{{ $json.benchmark_source }}\n\nBenchmark Confidence:\n{{ $json.benchmark_confidence }}\n\nPerformance Direction:\n{{ $json.direction }}\n\nCalculated External Benchmark Gap:\n{{ $json.gap_percentage }}%\n\nPerformance Status:\n{{ $json.performance_status }}\n\nSeverity:\n{{ $json.severity }}\n\nProvide:\n- a short benchmark gap summary\n- 2 to 3 potential causes to investigate\n- up to {{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.max_recommendations }} practical recommended actions\n- one short management comment","batching":{},"messages":{"messageValues":[{"message":"You are a procurement performance analyst.  Your job is to interpret supplied procurement KPI benchmark results and provide concise, management-ready analysis and practical recommendations.  RULES:  1. Treat the supplied numerical analysis as authoritative. Do not change or override: - actual value - benchmark value - gap percentage - performance status - severity  2. The supplied gap_percentage represents the percentage difference between the Actual Value and the External Benchmark only.  Do NOT describe gap_percentage as a difference from the KPI Target.  The KPI Target is provided only as additional business context. Do not calculate or infer a percentage difference against the KPI Target.  3. Do not invent company-specific facts.  4. Do not claim that another procurement problem exists unless that information is explicitly included in the supplied KPI context.  5. Likely causes must always be presented as potential causes, not confirmed facts.  Use wording such as: - Potential causes may include... - This can sometimes result from... - One area to investigate is...  6. Recommended actions must be practical and directly related to the supplied KPI.  7. Do not perform new calculations.  8. Do not introduce new benchmark values.  9. Keep the response concise and professional.  10. Output requirements: - gap_summary must be one string. - likely_causes must always be an array containing 2 to 3 separate strings. - recommended_actions must always be an array containing up to 3 separate strings. - management_comment must be one string. - Never combine likely causes into one paragraph. - Do not return fields outside the required structured output.\nDo not make claims about company profitability, financial performance,\noperational failure, or business impact unless those outcomes are\nexplicitly supported by the supplied KPI context.\n\nDescribe the result in terms of benchmark performance, procurement\nefficiency, cost opportunity, compliance, or process improvement only."}]},"promptType":"define","hasOutputParser":true},"typeVersion":1.9},{"id":"d73fdfa7-7de3-439e-9d84-799365a87472","name":"Prepare Benchmark Result Row","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[-80,608],"parameters":{"mode":"runOnceForEachItem","jsCode":"const ai = $json.output;\n\nconst benchmark = $('Calculate Benchmark Gap').item.json;\n\nconst completedStatus =\n  $('Load Benchmark Settings')\n    .first()\n    .json\n    .report_status_completed;\n\nconst now = new Date().toISOString();\n\nconst resultId =\n  `RESULT-${benchmark.kpi_code}-${benchmark.period}-${Date.now()}`;\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    result_id: resultId,\n    analysis_date: now,\n\n    kpi_record_id: benchmark.kpi_record_id,\n\n\n    period: benchmark.period,\n    business_unit: benchmark.business_unit,\n\n    kpi_code: benchmark.kpi_code,\n    kpi_name: benchmark.kpi_name,\n\n    actual_value: benchmark.actual_value,\n    benchmark_value: benchmark.benchmark_value,\n    unit: benchmark.unit,\n\n    direction: benchmark.direction,\n\n    absolute_gap: benchmark.absolute_gap,\n    gap_percentage: benchmark.gap_percentage,\n\n    performance_status: benchmark.performance_status,\n    severity: benchmark.severity,\n\n    gap_summary: ai.gap_summary,\n\n    likely_causes: Array.isArray(ai.likely_causes)\n      ? ai.likely_causes.join(' | ')\n      : String(ai.likely_causes || ''),\n\n    recommended_actions: Array.isArray(ai.recommended_actions)\n      ? ai.recommended_actions.join(' | ')\n      : String(ai.recommended_actions || ''),\n\n    priority: benchmark.severity,\n\n    management_comment: ai.management_comment,\n\n    ai_model: 'Google Gemini',\n\n    processing_status: completedStatus\n  }\n};"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"5c1a8c5f-0433-476f-8a51-f290d56f9c47","name":"Append Benchmark Result","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","position":[288,608],"parameters":{"columns":{"value":{"unit":"={{ $json.unit }}","period":"={{ $json.period }}","ai_model":"={{ $json.ai_model }}","kpi_code":"={{ $json.kpi_code }}","kpi_name":"={{ $json.kpi_name }}","priority":"={{ $json.priority }}","severity":"={{ $json.severity }}","direction":"={{ $json.direction }}","result_id":"={{ $json.result_id }}","gap_summary":"={{ $json.gap_summary }}","absolute_gap":"={{ $json.absolute_gap }}","actual_value":"={{ $json.actual_value }}","analysis_date":"={{ $json.analysis_date }}","business_unit":"={{ $json.business_unit }}","likely_causes":"={{ $json.likely_causes }}","gap_percentage":"={{ $json.gap_percentage }}","benchmark_value":"={{ $json.benchmark_value }}","processing_status":"={{ $json.processing_status }}","management_comment":"={{ $json.management_comment }}","performance_status":"={{ $json.performance_status }}","recommended_actions":"={{ $json.recommended_actions }}"},"schema":[{"id":"result_id","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"result_id","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"analysis_date","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"analysis_date","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"period","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"period","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"business_unit","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"business_unit","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"kpi_code","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"kpi_code","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"kpi_name","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"kpi_name","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"actual_value","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"actual_value","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"benchmark_value","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"benchmark_value","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"unit","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"unit","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"direction","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"direction","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"absolute_gap","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"absolute_gap","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"gap_percentage","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"gap_percentage","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"performance_status","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"performance_status","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"severity","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"severity","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"gap_summary","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"gap_summary","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"likely_causes","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"likely_causes","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"recommended_actions","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"recommended_actions","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"priority","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"priority","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"management_comment","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"management_comment","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"ai_model","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"ai_model","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"processing_status","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"processing_status","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true}],"mappingMode":"defineBelow","matchingColumns":[],"attemptToConvertTypes":false,"convertFieldsToString":false},"options":{},"operation":"append","sheetName":{"__rl":true,"mode":"list","value":448979579,"cachedResultUrl":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY/edit#gid=448979579","cachedResultName":"Benchmark_Results"},"documentId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"list","value":"1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY","cachedResultUrl":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY/edit?usp=drivesdk","cachedResultName":"Procurement_KPI_Benchmarking_Mock_Data"}},"typeVersion":4.7},{"id":"9f3940ba-25e6-4f66-885b-6209f50af88f","name":"Mark KPI as Processed","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","position":[496,608],"parameters":{"columns":{"value":{"status":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.processed_status }}","kpi_record_id":"={{ $('Prepare Benchmark Result Row').item.json.kpi_record_id }}"},"schema":[{"id":"kpi_record_id","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"kpi_record_id","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"kpi_code","type":"string","display":true,"removed":true,"required":false,"displayName":"kpi_code","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"kpi_name","type":"string","display":true,"removed":true,"required":false,"displayName":"kpi_name","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"period","type":"string","display":true,"removed":true,"required":false,"displayName":"period","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"business_unit","type":"string","display":true,"removed":true,"required":false,"displayName":"business_unit","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"actual_value","type":"string","display":true,"removed":true,"required":false,"displayName":"actual_value","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"unit","type":"string","display":true,"removed":true,"required":false,"displayName":"unit","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"target_value","type":"string","display":true,"removed":true,"required":false,"displayName":"target_value","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"status","type":"string","display":true,"required":false,"displayName":"status","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"data_source","type":"string","display":true,"removed":true,"required":false,"displayName":"data_source","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"row_number","type":"number","display":true,"removed":true,"readOnly":true,"required":false,"displayName":"row_number","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true}],"mappingMode":"defineBelow","matchingColumns":["kpi_record_id"],"attemptToConvertTypes":false,"convertFieldsToString":false},"options":{},"operation":"update","sheetName":{"__rl":true,"mode":"list","value":838784183,"cachedResultUrl":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY/edit#gid=838784183","cachedResultName":"Procurement_KPIs"},"documentId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"list","value":"1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY","cachedResultUrl":"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1Sw0ES-X9PR_fzoQLG9wYGYWMo_IsKb7KiVSouTWS-iY/edit?usp=drivesdk","cachedResultName":"Procurement_KPI_Benchmarking_Mock_Data"}},"typeVersion":4.7},{"id":"730ef841-f212-4321-bfe3-c9dd85d02fb8","name":"Is Significant Gap?","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[704,608],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"version":3,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"strict"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"319bf084-8e61-4061-9c1a-444a730b3400","operator":{"type":"boolean","operation":"true","singleValue":true},"leftValue":"={{ $('Calculate Benchmark Gap').item.json.benchmark_gap_detected }}","rightValue":""}]}},"typeVersion":2.3},{"id":"139662f8-7755-4976-8d8e-9af1f42cc621","name":"Prepare Leadership Alert","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[912,592],"parameters":{"mode":"runOnceForEachItem","jsCode":"const result = $('Prepare Benchmark Result Row').item.json;\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    alert_id: `ALERT-${result.kpi_code}-${result.period}-${Date.now()}`,\n    alert_date: new Date().toISOString(),\n\n    kpi_code: result.kpi_code,\n    kpi_name: result.kpi_name,\n\n    period: result.period,\n    business_unit: result.business_unit,\n\n    severity: result.severity,\n    priority: result.priority,\n\n    actual_value: result.actual_value,\n    benchmark_value: result.benchmark_value,\n    unit: result.unit,\n\n    gap_percentage: result.gap_percentage,\n\n    alert_title:\n      `${result.severity} Procurement KPI Gap - ${result.kpi_name}`,\n\n    alert_summary: result.gap_summary,\n\n    recommended_actions: result.recommended_actions,\n\n    management_comment: result.management_comment,\n\n    alert_status:\n  $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.alert_open_status\n  }\n};"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"1a898d71-1490-41b5-8e5c-75796accb62a","name":"Send Leadership Alert Email","type":"n8n-nodes-base.gmail","position":[1152,592],"webhookId":"67cf4fa1-2e6b-454f-a0e9-892d87956e6e","parameters":{"sendTo":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.leadership_email }}","message":"=<h2>{{ $json.alert_title }}</h2>  <p> A significant procurement KPI performance gap has been identified during the monthly benchmarking process. </p>  <table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\">   <tr>     <td><strong>KPI</strong></td>     <td>{{ $json.kpi_name }}</td>   </tr>   <tr>     <td><strong>Period</strong></td>     <td>{{ $json.period }}</td>   </tr>   <tr>     <td><strong>Business Unit</strong></td>     <td>{{ $json.business_unit }}</td>   </tr>   <tr>     <td><strong>Actual Value</strong></td>     <td>{{ $json.actual_value }} {{ $json.unit }}</td>   </tr>   <tr>     <td><strong>External Benchmark</strong></td>     <td>{{ $json.benchmark_value }} {{ $json.unit }}</td>   </tr>   <tr>     <td><strong>Benchmark Gap</strong></td>     <td>{{ $json.gap_percentage }}%</td>   </tr>   <tr>     <td><strong>Severity</strong></td>     <td>{{ $json.severity }}</td>   </tr> </table>  <h3>Gap Summary</h3> <p>{{ $json.alert_summary }}</p> <h3>Recommended Actions</h3>\n<p>\n• {{ $json.recommended_actions.replace(/\\s*\\|\\s*/g, '<br>• ') }}\n</p> <h3>Management Comment</h3> <p>{{ $json.management_comment }}</p>  <p> This alert was generated automatically by the Procurement KPI Benchmarking & Gap Analysis workflow. </p>","options":{},"subject":"={{ $json.alert_title }}"},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"f004bbef-ce89-4a20-95fa-5a5a178d5362","name":"No Leadership Alert Required","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[1008,880],"parameters":{"options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"2fbf7b49-5491-408a-8767-518f3b44d973","name":"alert_required","type":"boolean","value":false},{"id":"30c51703-ea5e-4e67-8450-5464c4de3d16","name":"completion_status","type":"string","value":"Completed"},{"id":"d14bef1f-5d34-48d9-9d24-e3f461be9549","name":"completion_message","type":"string","value":"No leadership alert required for this KPI."}]}},"typeVersion":3.4},{"id":"9e21ed61-6969-4d52-8d03-3c0009da773d","name":"KPI Definition Found?","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[-2592,992],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"version":3,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"strict"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"c10f09c5-bfd2-40cb-8f4b-23162232cec2","operator":{"type":"boolean","operation":"true","singleValue":true},"leftValue":"={{ Boolean($json.kpi_code) }}","rightValue":""}]}},"typeVersion":2.3},{"id":"19f36644-2c4f-4c90-940f-23185c92236d","name":"Handle Missing KPI Definition","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[-2352,1168],"parameters":{"options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"6a712ac9-86fb-40a5-a5fa-67f583e9974c","name":"processing_status","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.review_required_status }}"},{"id":"6bf85ab4-9429-4e48-b9e8-093f3b09e2e0","name":"error_type","type":"string","value":"Missing KPI Definition"},{"id":"e89480ad-1159-42a6-84b2-3115607e181b","name":"error_message","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.missing_definition_message }}"},{"id":"5f1d787e-9517-4723-93ec-213a023dd02f","name":"should_continue","type":"boolean","value":false},{"id":"2f72e3b4-bb21-4888-9f0e-2b12b43b4209","name":"kpi_code","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Get Ready Procurement KPIs').item.json.kpi_code }}"},{"id":"49714005-4ae5-4d8f-babe-a1bca4c43ac2","name":"kpi_record_id","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Get Ready Procurement KPIs').item.json.kpi_record_id }}"}]}},"typeVersion":3.4,"alwaysOutputData":true},{"id":"fe71afdf-1ae9-4619-b251-34f772d65bda","name":"External Benchmark Found?","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[-2064,832],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"version":3,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"strict"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"5a9410d2-fe2c-4cf2-a50a-be53c053abab","operator":{"type":"boolean","operation":"true","singleValue":true},"leftValue":"={{ Boolean($json.benchmark_id) }}","rightValue":""}]}},"typeVersion":2.3},{"id":"bdd63d7b-a1e1-4ebb-8ada-bb8982834514","name":"Handle Missing External Benchmark","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[-1600,1024],"parameters":{"options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"73c9bbdb-1f54-4d98-b969-be9fd2c0e660","name":"processing_status","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.review_required_status }}"},{"id":"ffd7858b-d53f-43e6-bee7-0b8685193cb5","name":"error_type","type":"string","value":"Missing External Benchmark"},{"id":"e625c055-530c-4558-b564-6dacf5fbbf4c","name":"error_message","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.missing_benchmark_message }}"},{"id":"b7e496ad-350b-4db5-9d53-ef5c97134158","name":"should_continue","type":"boolean","value":false},{"id":"da2cea66-2256-40f9-94b9-2c2b907f0597","name":"kpi_code","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Get Ready Procurement KPIs').item.json.kpi_code }}"},{"id":"052863ce-c548-404a-a0c3-22b26caf9a85","name":"kpi_record_id","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Get Ready Procurement KPIs').item.json.kpi_record_id }}"}]}},"typeVersion":3.4},{"id":"115f1fd3-c178-4b6d-8586-1a7719aa8ddf","name":"Validate Benchmark Inputs","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[-1440,624],"parameters":{"mode":"runOnceForEachItem","jsCode":"const item = $json;\n\nconst errors = [];\n\n// Helper: reject null, undefined, empty string,\n// and anything that cannot be converted to a finite number.\nconst isValidNumericValue = (value) => {\n  if (\n    value === null ||\n    value === undefined ||\n    value === ''\n  ) {\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  const converted = Number(value);\n\n  return Number.isFinite(converted);\n};\n\n//\n// 1. Actual KPI value\n//\nif (!isValidNumericValue(item.actual_value)) {\n  errors.push('Actual KPI value is invalid.');\n}\n\n//\n// 2. External benchmark\n//\nif (!isValidNumericValue(item.benchmark_value)) {\n  errors.push('External benchmark value is invalid.');\n} else if (Number(item.benchmark_value) === 0) {\n  errors.push('External benchmark value cannot be zero.');\n}\n\n//\n// 3. Warning threshold\n//\nif (!isValidNumericValue(item.warning_threshold_pct)) {\n  errors.push('Warning threshold is invalid.');\n}\n\n//\n// 4. Critical threshold\n//\nif (!isValidNumericValue(item.critical_threshold_pct)) {\n  errors.push('Critical threshold is invalid.');\n}\n\n//\n// 5. Threshold relationship\n//\nif (\n  isValidNumericValue(item.warning_threshold_pct) &&\n  isValidNumericValue(item.critical_threshold_pct)\n) {\n  const warningThreshold =\n    Number(item.warning_threshold_pct);\n\n  const criticalThreshold =\n    Number(item.critical_threshold_pct);\n\n  if (warningThreshold > criticalThreshold) {\n    errors.push(\n      'Warning threshold cannot be greater than critical threshold.'\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    ...item,\n\n    benchmark_inputs_valid:\n      errors.length === 0,\n\n    validation_errors:\n      errors\n  }\n};"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"5d9ccf07-1d36-4ced-869c-1738db80644b","name":"Benchmark Inputs Valid?","type":"n8n-nodes-base.if","position":[-1200,624],"parameters":{"options":{},"conditions":{"options":{"version":3,"leftValue":"","caseSensitive":true,"typeValidation":"strict"},"combinator":"and","conditions":[{"id":"3569ab24-4f0a-4905-9597-9daf1d5ac05f","operator":{"type":"boolean","operation":"true","singleValue":true},"leftValue":"={{ $json.benchmark_inputs_valid }}","rightValue":""}]}},"typeVersion":2.3},{"id":"07d63c20-e169-43b6-a52b-df811f4da0e0","name":"Handle Invalid Benchmark Data","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[-928,896],"parameters":{"options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"2477648d-8c49-4504-8998-35f95ff39999","name":"processing_status","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.review_required_status }}"},{"id":"bf15463c-854b-477b-af9d-d37ec9f26c31","name":"error_type","type":"string","value":"Invalid Benchmark Data"},{"id":"3455c7db-7228-46a6-857d-6789b6a10d97","name":"should_continue","type":"boolean","value":false},{"id":"a6a3cb57-4442-44c3-bc5f-4602ff559f02","name":"error_message","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Validate Benchmark Inputs').item.json.validation_errors.join(' | ') }}"},{"id":"c9fe4a8a-5aff-4460-b217-f8c501252f7e","name":"kpi_code","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Get Ready Procurement KPIs').item.json.kpi_code }}"},{"id":"cc10670b-1c97-48c7-9a4b-0cb42e372caa","name":"kpi_record_id","type":"string","value":"={{ $('Get Ready Procurement KPIs').item.json.kpi_record_id }}"}]}},"typeVersion":3.4},{"id":"f659dd38-b4e9-4b60-b64a-5a4aabca9081","name":"Build Monthly Benchmark Report","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[416,1072],"parameters":{"jsCode":"const rows = $input.all().map(item => item.json);\n\nif (rows.length === 0) {\n  return [];\n}\n\nconst first = rows[0];\n\nconst totalKpis = rows.length;\n\nconst aboveBenchmark =\n  rows.filter(r => r.performance_status === 'Above Benchmark').length;\n\nconst nearBenchmark =\n  rows.filter(r => r.performance_status === 'Near Benchmark').length;\n\nconst belowBenchmark =\n  rows.filter(r => r.performance_status === 'Below Benchmark').length;\n\nconst criticalCount =\n  rows.filter(r => r.severity === 'Critical').length;\n\nconst highCount =\n  rows.filter(r => r.severity === 'High').length;\n\nconst mediumCount =\n  rows.filter(r => r.severity === 'Medium').length;\n\nconst lowCount =\n  rows.filter(r => r.severity === 'Low').length;\n\n// Highest below-benchmark gaps first\nconst topGaps = [...rows]\n  .filter(r => r.performance_status === 'Below Benchmark')\n  .sort((a, b) => Number(b.gap_percentage) - Number(a.gap_percentage))\n  .slice(0, 3);\n\n// Build KPI table rows\nconst kpiTableRows = rows.map(r => `\n  <tr>\n    <td>${r.kpi_name}</td>\n    <td>${r.actual_value} ${r.unit}</td>\n    <td>${r.benchmark_value} ${r.unit}</td>\n    <td>${r.gap_percentage}%</td>\n    <td>${r.performance_status}</td>\n    <td>${r.severity}</td>\n  </tr>\n`).join('');\n\n// Build top-gap section\nconst topGapHtml = topGaps.length\n  ? topGaps.map((r, index) => `\n      <li>\n        <strong>${index + 1}. ${r.kpi_name}</strong>\n        — ${r.gap_percentage}% gap (${r.severity})\n        <br>\n        ${r.gap_summary}\n      </li>\n    `).join('')\n  : '<li>No significant below-benchmark gaps were identified.</li>';\nconst reportTitlePrefix =\n  $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.report_title_prefix;\n\nconst reportHtml = `\n<h2>${reportTitlePrefix} - ${first.period}</h2>\n\n<p>\nThis monthly report summarizes procurement KPI performance against\nthe configured external peer benchmarks.\n</p>\n\n<h3>Executive Summary</h3>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"\n       style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\">\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>KPIs Analyzed</strong></td>\n    <td>${totalKpis}</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>Above Benchmark</strong></td>\n    <td>${aboveBenchmark}</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>Near Benchmark</strong></td>\n    <td>${nearBenchmark}</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>Below Benchmark</strong></td>\n    <td>${belowBenchmark}</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>Critical Gaps</strong></td>\n    <td>${criticalCount}</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>KPI Benchmark Results</h3>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"\n       style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\">\n  <tr>\n    <th>KPI</th>\n    <th>Actual</th>\n    <th>Benchmark</th>\n    <th>Gap</th>\n    <th>Status</th>\n    <th>Severity</th>\n  </tr>\n  ${kpiTableRows}\n</table>\n\n<h3>Top Performance Gaps</h3>\n\n<ol>\n${topGapHtml}\n</ol>\n\n<p>\nThis report was generated automatically by the\nProcurement KPI Benchmarking workflow.\n</p>\n`;\n\nreturn [\n  {\n    json: {\n      report_id:\n        `REPORT-${first.period}-${Date.now()}`,\n\n      generated_at:\n        new Date().toISOString(),\n\n      period:\n        first.period,\n\n      business_unit:\n        first.business_unit,\n\n      total_kpis:\n        totalKpis,\n\n      above_benchmark_count:\n        aboveBenchmark,\n\n      near_benchmark_count:\n        nearBenchmark,\n\n      below_benchmark_count:\n        belowBenchmark,\n\n      critical_count:\n        criticalCount,\n\n      high_count:\n        highCount,\n\n      medium_count:\n        mediumCount,\n\n      low_count:\n        lowCount,\n\n      report_title:\n        `${$('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.report_title_prefix} - ${first.period}`,\n\n      report_html:\n        reportHtml\n    }\n  }\n];"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"bf9bffc7-6314-41cc-a23a-50b3468fe9c5","name":"Send Monthly Benchmark Report","type":"n8n-nodes-base.gmail","position":[720,1072],"webhookId":"4abd71fa-8397-45a6-8cf7-7b837a58be47","parameters":{"sendTo":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').first().json.monthly_report_email }}","message":"={{ $json.report_html }}","options":{},"subject":"={{ $json.report_title }}"},"typeVersion":2.2},{"id":"3150b5a2-f78b-4319-955f-cba493e698ae","name":"Sticky Note","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-4592,688],"parameters":{"width":752,"height":688,"content":"# Procurement Metrics Benchmarking Workflow\n\nThis workflow runs monthly and benchmarks procurement KPIs against configured peer or industry values. It loads Ready KPI records, validates KPI definitions and benchmark data, calculates performance gaps, and uses Google Gemini to generate concise causes and recommended actions.\n\nSuccessful results are stored in Google Sheets. Significant gaps trigger leadership email alerts, while a consolidated monthly KPI benchmark report is generated and emailed for management review. Invalid or incomplete records are stopped safely for review.\n\n## Setup steps\n\n1. Connect Google Sheets, Gmail, and Google Gemini credentials.\n2. Configure the required Google Sheets workbook and worksheet mappings.\n3. Update reusable values in `Load Benchmark Settings`, including statuses, thresholds, email recipients, and report settings.\n4. Configure the monthly schedule trigger.\n5. Ensure KPI definitions and external benchmarks are active and available.\n6. Test with at least one KPI marked `Ready` before activating the workflow."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"9bba6d6e-d96d-4d95-af5f-c181ca154273","name":"Sticky Note1","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-3776,688],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":608,"height":688,"content":"### Trigger & Configuration\n\nRuns the workflow on the configured monthly schedule. Centralized settings control KPI statuses, benchmark flags, thresholds, email recipients, recommendation limits, and report settings."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"7139af63-83b3-4c2b-85bd-aa5724b7228e","name":"Sticky Note2","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-3088,688],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1248,"height":688,"content":"### KPI & Benchmark Retrieval\n\nLoads Ready KPI records, checks active KPI definitions, and retrieves matching external benchmark data. Missing definitions or benchmarks are routed to review handling instead of continuing."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"cf9bb21c-caaa-4cf7-99cb-7236e8ed02f1","name":"Sticky Note3","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-1760,384],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1072,"height":992,"content":"### Validation & Benchmark Calculation\n\nBuilds the comparison context, validates required numeric inputs, and calculates benchmark gap, performance status, and severity using deterministic workflow logic."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"cb6516e5-9d7c-4f4c-9bf5-b1d9cbf51363","name":"Sticky Note4","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-592,384],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":688,"height":624,"content":"### AI Analysis & Recommendations\n\nGoogle Gemini interprets the calculated KPI result and returns structured gap summaries, potential causes, recommended actions, and a management comment without changing the calculated benchmark values."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"7b9bad87-20e7-4646-a00c-ce403e40a380","name":"Sticky Note5","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[208,384],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":1152,"height":992,"content":"### Results, Alerts & Reporting\n\nStores completed KPI analysis, marks source records as Processed, sends leadership alerts for significant gaps, and generates a consolidated monthly benchmark report for management review."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"34eec4c8-74c7-46b2-8de9-f17f3d9007d1","name":"Gemini Model for KPI Analysis","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini","position":[-528,816],"parameters":{"options":{}},"credentials":{"googlePalmApi":{"id":"33FrMvULTwg001u9","name":"Google Gemini (MaryPhelps) AiStudio Builder AWS"}},"typeVersion":1.1},{"id":"c18cc28c-e822-4842-9b22-e3d5f898c792","name":"Parse Structured KPI Analysis","type":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.outputParserStructured","position":[-240,816],"parameters":{"schemaType":"manual","inputSchema":"{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"gap_summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"A concise management-ready explanation of the supplied KPI benchmark gap.\"\n    },\n    \"likely_causes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"Potential procurement causes to investigate. These must not be presented as confirmed facts.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 2,\n      \"maxItems\": 3\n    },\n    \"recommended_actions\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"Specific and practical procurement actions relevant to the KPI.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"maxItems\": 3\n    },\n    \"management_comment\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"One concise executive-level statement about the importance of addressing the KPI.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"gap_summary\",\n    \"likely_causes\",\n    \"recommended_actions\",\n    \"management_comment\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}"},"typeVersion":1.3},{"id":"fcf9b692-dd51-4e79-9937-4329e502911e","name":"Get Ready Procurement KPIs","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","position":[-3040,992],"parameters":{"options":{},"filtersUI":{"values":[{"lookupValue":"={{ $('Load Benchmark Settings').item.json.ready_status 